  <title>Incoming invoices</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Incoming invoices</gui></guiseq>
  records a bill from a service provider and pays it in one step. Bills for
  goods ordered on a purchase order go through <link xref="unprocessed_po"/>
  instead. The same window is the <gui>Payment</gui> tab of <link
  xref="shipping_info"/>.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the service provider. Only contacts marked as a service
    provider are listed; <gui>Service Provider</gui> opens the contacts window
    to mark one.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Invoice number / description</gui>, the
    <gui>Amount</gui>, and choose the <gui>Date</gui>. <gui>Attach</gui> keeps
    a scan of the bill; see <link xref="pdf_attachment"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Split the amount over the expense accounts it belongs to. Add a
    row with the add button beside the list, type its <gui>Percent</gui> or
    <gui>Amount</gui>, choose its <gui>Expense Account</gui> and add a
    <gui>Remark</gui>. The equalize button splits the amount evenly over the
    rows; right click a row and choose <gui>Balance this row</gui> to give it
    whatever the other rows leave.</p></item>
    <item><p>Pay it, as below.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <section id="pay">
  <title>Paying</title>
  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Pay with cash / credit card</gui>: choose the account
    <gui>from cash account</gui> and click <gui>Cash payment</gui>, or choose
    the card <gui>from credit card</gui> and click <gui>Credit card
    payment</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Pay from bank account</gui>: choose the bank account. For a
    transfer or debit, type the <gui>Transaction number</gui> and click
    <gui>Transfer payment</gui>. To pay by check, type the <gui>Check
    number</gui> and click <gui>Print cheque &amp; post payment</gui>, or
    <gui>Post cheque payment</gui> for a check written by hand. Checking
    <gui>Cancel printing and posting</gui> in the print dialog stops the
    payment.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>The pay buttons say what is missing until the bill can be paid, for
  instance <gui>Invoice amount does not match payment</gui> when the rows do
  not add up to the amount, or <gui>Missing expense accounts</gui>.</p>
  </section>

</page>
